# ============================================================================
# Lustia auth-service — manual test book
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - auth-service running on :8080 (source run-local.sh && go run ./cmd/auth)
#   - Mailpit running on :1025 SMTP + :8025 UI
#   - Postgres running on :5432, all 8 migrations applied
#   - Two seeded users:
#       admin@lustia.local  / ResetViaEmail789!   (super admin, __platform__)
#       alice@acme-spa.example / Staff2026!       (tenant_admin @ acme-spa)
#
# How to run:
#   - VSCode / Kiro / Cursor with REST Client extension → "Send Request" above
#     each block
#   - JetBrains IDEs → green ▶ in the gutter
#   - Without an IDE:  grab a block, paste as `curl` (syntax is close)
#
# Variables marked {{...}} are auto-filled by earlier requests in the same file.
# ============================================================================

@host = http://localhost:8080
@mailpit = http://localhost:8025


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 0. Health / discovery
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### readyz
GET {{host}}/readyz

### healthz
GET {{host}}/healthz

### JWKS (public key — verify RS256 JWTs offline)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/.well-known/jwks.json


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. SUPER ADMIN flow  (tenant_slug = "__platform__")
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### @name login_super
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@lustia.local",
  "password": "ResetViaEmail789!",
  "tenant_slug": "__platform__"
}

###
@super_token = {{login_super.response.body.access_token}}
@super_refresh = {{login_super.response.body.refresh_token}}

### /auth/me (super admin — tenant_id is null)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{super_token}}

### /admin/users — super admin sees all tenants
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{super_token}}

### /admin/roles — should return 6 seeded roles
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{super_token}}

### refresh the super-admin token (rotation; old refresh is revoked)
### @name refresh_super
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{super_refresh}}"
}

### logout (invalidates refresh token server-side)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{super_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{super_refresh}}"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. TENANT STAFF flow  (alice @ acme-spa)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### @name login_alice
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@acme-spa.example",
  "password": "Staff2026!",
  "tenant_slug": "acme-spa"
}

###
@alice_token = {{login_alice.response.body.access_token}}
@alice_refresh = {{login_alice.response.body.refresh_token}}

### /auth/me as alice — shows acme-spa tenant info
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token}}

### /admin/users as alice — RLS-scoped: only sees users in acme-spa (1 row)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token}}

### /admin/roles as alice — roles are platform reference data, all 6 visible
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token}}

### IDOR probe — alice attempts to load the super admin by UUID → must 404
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/users/a0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token}}

### refresh alice's token
### @name refresh_alice
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{alice_refresh}}"
}

###
@alice_token2 = {{refresh_alice.response.body.access_token}}

### use the NEW token — works
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token2}}

### use the OLD refresh token — must be REFRESH_REVOKED (single-use rotation)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{alice_refresh}}"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. FORGOT / RESET PASSWORD  (checks mail via Mailpit)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### forgot password — always 204, anti-enumeration
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/password/forgot
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@acme-spa.example",
  "tenant_slug": "acme-spa"
}

### Open the Mailpit UI in a browser to see the message:
###   http://localhost:8025
### → click the top message → copy the token from "?token=..." in the body.

### Or hit the API to list messages + extract token:
GET {{mailpit}}/api/v1/messages

### Replace the token below with the one you copied from Mailpit:
### ⚠ tokens are single-use + expire in 60 minutes.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/password/reset
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_MAILPIT_HERE",
  "new_password": "StaffRotated2026!"
}

### try the OLD password → must 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@acme-spa.example",
  "password": "Staff2026!",
  "tenant_slug": "acme-spa"
}

### ... and the NEW password works
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@acme-spa.example",
  "password": "StaffRotated2026!",
  "tenant_slug": "acme-spa"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. CHANGE OWN PASSWORD  (self-service, requires JWT)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Must use the latest alice token ({{alice_token2}} from block 2,
### OR log in again and capture a fresh one above).

POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "old_password": "StaffRotated2026!",
  "new_password": "StaffAgain2026!"
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. ADMIN: create a user inside acme-spa  (alice is tenant_admin)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### Need the tenant_admin role UUID once — fetch the role list:
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token}}

### Then create a therapist-role user (paste tenant_admin or therapist role_id
### from the list above into role_ids):
POST {{host}}/api/v1/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@acme-spa.example",
  "full_name": "Bob Therapist",
  "phone": "+628120000000",
  "role_ids": ["PASTE_THERAPIST_ROLE_UUID_HERE"],
  "branch_ids": [],
  "initial_password": "BobInitial2026!"
}

### list users — should see alice + bob
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token}}

### login as bob — note must_change_password=true on admin-created users
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@acme-spa.example",
  "password": "BobInitial2026!",
  "tenant_slug": "acme-spa"
}

### bob cannot hit /admin/users — he's a therapist, no user.read permission
### (replace with the access_token from his login response)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_BOBS_TOKEN_HERE


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. ERROR PATHS  (verify sanity)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### wrong password → 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@acme-spa.example",
  "password": "WrongPassword",
  "tenant_slug": "acme-spa"
}

### unknown tenant → 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS (not TENANT_NOT_FOUND — anti-enum)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@acme-spa.example",
  "password": "anything",
  "tenant_slug": "nonexistent"
}

### no bearer token → 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me

### malformed bearer → 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: NotBearer foo

### tampered token (flip a char) → 401 TOKEN_INVALID
GET {{host}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token}}X
